<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Muhammad of Ghor</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">assassinated <a href="/years/1206">1206</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Muhammad of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghor">Ghor</a> was a ruler of the Ghurid dynasty who conquered much of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> in the late twelfth century. His victory at the second Battle of Tarain in 1192 opened the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ganges-plain">Ganges plain</a> to Muslim rule. After his assassination in 1206, his general Qutb al-Din Aibak founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi-sultanate">Delhi Sultanate</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/muhammad-of-ghor.jpg" alt="Muhammad of Ghor" width="320" height="154" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CNG Coins · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mu%27izz_al-Din_Muhammad._AH_599-602_AD_1171-1206.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
